ions. XML is a World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) specification and is a subset of Standard Generalized Markup Language (SGML).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1209">XML</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1229800">XML</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14842_1209_1247437"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A markup language for describing and exchanging structured data in a format that is independent of operating systems and applications. XML is a World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) specification and is a subset of Standard Generalized Markup Language (SGML).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1209">XML</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1247437">എക്സ്റ്റന്‍സിബിള്‍ അടയാളപ്പെടുത്തല്‍ ഭാഷ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14843_318774_490639"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The $ character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318774">dollar sign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490639">ഡോളര്‍ ചിഹ്നം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14843_318775_490639"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The $ character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318775">DOLLAR SIGN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490639">ഡോളര്‍ ചിഹ്നം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14845_157682_489947"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows security feature that locks a user account if a number of failed logon attempts occur within a specified amount of time, based on security policy lockout settings. Locked accounts cannot log on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="157682">account lockout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489947">അക്കൌണ്ട് ലോക്കൌട്ട്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14848_253634_489410"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line or row of characters used to lead the eye from a data label to a data point, or from a callout to the appropriate part of an illustration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253634">leader line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489410">ലീഡര്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14848_253634_490258"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line or row of characters used to lead the eye from a data label to a data point, or from a callout to the appropriate part of an illustration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253634">leader line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490258">ലീഡര്‍ വര</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14848_73800_489410"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line or row of characters used to lead the eye from a data label to a data point, or from a callout to the appropriate part of an illustration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73800">leader</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489410">ലീഡര്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14848_73800_490258"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line or row of characters used to lead the eye from a data label to a data point, or from a callout to the appropriate part of an illustration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73800">leader</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490258">ലീഡര്‍ വര</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14854_359997_490838"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field in a table that draws data from another table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="359997">Lookup field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490838">ലുക്കപ്പ് മണ്ഡലം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14856_370913_1805315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a cascading style sheet style definition (or style rule), the HTML element linked to a particular set of style properties and values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="370913">selector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1805315">సెలక్టర్</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14866_396930_1961010"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A distribution group that uses recipient filters and conditions to derive its membership at the time the message is sent.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="396930">dynamic distribution group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1961010">ഡൈനാമിക് വിതരണ ഗ്രൂപ്പ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14867_252650_1241936"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An organizational work model that emphasizes the use of small, cohesive teams of role specialists who communicate on an equal basis in the accomplishment of their individual and group tasks. This work model contrasts to that of the traditional top-down, linear-structure work model, and has been functionally proven in a variety of different organizations, cultures, and project sizes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="252650">team of peers</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241936">തുല്യരുടെ ടീം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1488_136966_489790"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A row in the upper part of the Macro window in which you enter macro names, actions, conditions, and comments associated with a particular macro or macro group.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136966">action row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489790">ക്രിയാ വരി</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14885_397156_1961025"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Exchange 2007 graphical user interface (GUI) from which administrators can perform tasks to configure and manage Exchange servers. The Exchange Management Console is based on Windows Microsoft Management Console (MMC) 3.0.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397156">Exchange Management Console</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1961025">Exchange മാനേജുമെന്‍റ് കണ്‍സോള്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14886_321129_490681"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that helps improve the recognition of a user's touch flicks by a process in which the user's touch flicks are analyzed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="321129">touch training</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="