ected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15549_316259_490556"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The output created in desktop publishing applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="316259">publication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490556">പ്രസിദ്ധീകരണം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1555_187689_1241213"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The assignment of more than one function to a particular operator, with the implication that the operation performed will vary depending on the data type (operands) involved. Some languages, such as Ada and C++, specifically allow for operator overloading.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="187689">operator overloading</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241213">ഓപ്പറേറ്റര്‍ ഓവര്‍ലോഡ് ചെയ്യല്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15551_96356_489581"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of instructions for retrieving specific data from a large set, usually with multiple conditions. No list is displayed until you run the query.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="96356">query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489581">ചോദ്യം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15554_464503_1242226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A share that has been added to the Virtual Machine Manager library. To be available for use in creating virtual machines, a resource must be stored on a library share and must be added to the Virtual Machine Manager library. When a library server is added to Virtual Machine Manager, shares on the library server are automatically discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="464503">library share</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1242226">ലൈബ്രറി പങ്കിടല്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1556_187963_1241214"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The tool that creates instances of a project's objects, calls their methods, and evaluates the results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="187963">Object Test Bench</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241214">OTB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun