ting to a log when configured by a managed object format (MOF) file or a script.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="661880">standard consumer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1242148">സ്റ്റാന്‍ഡേര്‍ഡ് ഉപഭോക്താവ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19598_661882_1242149"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A template for a type of managed object. WMI classes define the basic units of management. For example, the Win32_LogicalDisk class is a template for all logical disks that occur in the Windows environment. In this case, WMI uses the class template to generate an instance of Win32_LogicalDisk for each disk installed on a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="661882">WMI class</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1242149">WMI ക്ലാസ്സ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19599_661883_1242150"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A class that the CIM Object Manager defines to support core features such as event notification, security, and localization. A system class is automatically defined in each namespace.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="661883">system class</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote 