</termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31299_1598409_1640611"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Hyper-V technology that runs on the Windows Client operating system, rather than Windows Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1598409">Client Hyper-V</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1640611">ക്ലയന്‍റ് Hyper-V</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31304_1598622_1640723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability for IT pros to define how users access a system based on dynamic qualities, such as a user's location or role.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1598622">dynamic access control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1640723">ഡൈനാമിക് പ്രവേശന നിയന്ത്രണം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="31305_1598623_1640771"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows feature designed to help users avoid data loss by automatically saving versions of files and copies of deleted files so that users can recover them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1598623">File History</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotS