ufacturing process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2898945">Factory Orchestrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899042">ഫാക്ടറി ഓർക്കസ്ട്രേറ്റർ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2899583_2900040"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899583">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900040">Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2899583_2949292"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899583">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949292">Education Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2949265_2900040"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949265">Education Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900040">Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51505_2949265_2949292"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams for Education that provides the user with at-a-glance data views to help them monitor their students' Teams activity, including overall digital engagement, assignment turn-in, communication activity, and grade distribution and trends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949265">Education Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2949292">Education Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51506_2899584_2900058"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The video conferencing mode in Microsoft Teams in which participants' video feeds are combined on the screen in such a way as to give the participants the impression that they are all in the same physical space together.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899584">Together mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900058">ഒരുമ മോഡ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51507_2899585_2900042"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The view in Microsoft Teams that allows the user to see up to 49 video feeds at once.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899585">Large gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900042">വലിയ ഗാലറി</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51508_2899586_2900039"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The view in Microsoft Teams that allows the user to see up to 9 video feeds at once.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899586">Gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900039">ഗാലറി</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51509_2899587_2900046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A billing model wherein an associated payment method is charged automatically over set periods of time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899587">recurring billing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900046">ആവർത്തക ബില്ലിംഗ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5151_228751_490106"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A real-time communication session between two or more users, which can involve IM, video, or audio.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228751">conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490106">സംഭാഷണം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51510_2899588_2900049"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of all-in-one dedicated Teams devices featuring an ambient touchscreen and a hands-free experience powered by Cortana that brings together the user's favorite Teams features: chat, meetings, calls, calendar, and files into a single device, promoting human connection in the remote workplace.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2899588">Teams display</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900049">Teams പ്രദർശനം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51543_2900640_2900812"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The dashboard in Microsoft Teams that provides the user with analytics about teams that they are a member or owner of, including data about user and guest volume as well as messaging activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900640">Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2900812">ഇൻസൈറ്റുകൾ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5155_237798_1241390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A deliverable of the planning phase for a development project. It consolidates feature team and role plans. The master project plan includes a budget plan, capacity plan, communications plan, deployment plan, development plan, pilot plan, purchasing and facilities plan, security plan, test plan, and training plan.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237798">master project plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241390">മാസ്റ്റര്‍ പ്രോജക്റ്റ് പദ്ധതി</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51563_2901221_2901289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A third-party device (such as a camera, headset, phone, or room accessory) that has been certified via the Microsoft device Certification Program to provide a compatible experience when used with specific Microsoft software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901221">certified device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901289">സാക്ഷ്യപ്പെടുത്തിയ ഉപകരണം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5157_40421_1241391"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A relative measure of the data-processing capacity of a particular central processing unit (CPU), usually measured in megahertz.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="40421">CPU speed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241391">CPU വേഗത</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51578_2901804_2901920"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Feature (either built into Windows or available as the Windows Lookup app) to allow users to select a word or group of words and look up more information, definition or translation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901804">Lookup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2901920">തിരഞ്ഞു നോക്കൽ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_489926"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154233">Layer Two Tunneling Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489926">ലെയര്‍ ടു ടണലിംഗ് പ്രോട്ടോക്കോള്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_154233_490579"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154233">Layer Two Tunneling Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490579">L2TP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_318115_489926"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318115">L2TP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489926">ലെയര്‍ ടു ടണലിംഗ് പ്രോട്ടോക്കോള്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5158_318115_490579"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An industry-standard Internet tunneling protocol that provides encapsulation for sending Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) frames across packet-oriented media. For IP networks, L2TP traffic is sent as User Datagram Protocol (UDP) messages. In Microsoft operating systems, L2TP is used in conjunction with Internet Protocol security (IPSec) as a virtual private network (VPN) technology to provide remote access or router-to-router VPN connections. L2TP is described in RFC 2661.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318115">L2TP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="490579">L2TP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51586_2902141_2902237"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A style in Word that shows text with a dotted underline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902141">Smart Hyperlink</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902237">സ്‌മാർട്ട് ഹൈപ്പർലിങ്ക്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51587_2902142_2902240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A style in Word that shows text as blue with a blue underline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902142">SmartLink</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902240">സ്‌മാർട്ട് ലിങ്ക്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51589_2902145_2902232"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A conceptual container that allows a company administrator to restrict the users and groups that an admin can manage to only those in a specific department, region, or any segment that their organization defines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902145">administrative unit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902232">അഡ്‌മിനിസ്‌ട്രേറ്റീവ് യൂണിറ്റ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51589_2910377_2902232"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A conceptual container that allows a company administrator to restrict the users and groups that an admin can manage to only those in a specific department, region, or any segment that their organization defines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2910377">AU</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902232">അഡ്‌മിനിസ്‌ട്രേറ്റീവ് യൂണിറ്റ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51593_2902151_2902235"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An isolated group within an organizational structure that has little to no interaction with other groups, often leading to a lack of collaboration and other negative outcomes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902151">silo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902235">സൈലോ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51606_2902290_2902736"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The phone feature that allows the user to view, send, receive, and download SMS and MMS text messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902290">Messages</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902736">സന്ദേശങ്ങൾ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51608_2902292_2902735"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The phone feature that allows the user to make and receive calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902292">Calls</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902735">കോളുകൾ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51609_2902293_2902737"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The phone feature that allows the user to control notification settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902293">Notifications</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902737">അറിയിപ്പുകൾ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="51610_2902294_2902734"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows users to access the apps installed on their phone or other mobile device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902294">Apps</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2902734">ആപ്പുകൾ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage"