ig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5348_2765047_1877909"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The banner near the top of an open email message, appointment, contact, or task that indicates if a message has been replied to or forwarded and that provides the online status of a contact who is using instant messaging.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2765047">infobar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1877909">ഇന്‍‌ഫോബാര്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53499_3046570_3046612"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app within the Teams client that contains functionality from both the Microsoft 365 and Teams admin centers and allows admin-type roles to manage app settings directly from the Teams app to improve end-user experience across Microsoft Teams and the Microsoft 365 suite.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3046570">Admin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3046612">അഡ്‍മിൻ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53500_3046571_3046619"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A business initiative to be accomplished, a large body of work that spans across releases.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig