">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2599908">മാസിക</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="800_879_2599906"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An electronic publication distributed primarily through the World Wide Web, rather than as an ink-on-paper magazine.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="879">web magazine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2599906">ഇലക്‌ട്രോണിക് മാസിക</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="800_879_2599908"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An electronic publication distributed primarily through the World Wide Web, rather than as an ink-on-paper magazine.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="879">web magazine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2599908">മാസിക</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8013_97176_1241534"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A condition in which two or more threads can reach and execute a block of code, and the program outcome changes radically depending on which thread reaches the code first. A race condition is benign if all outcomes are valid. However, race conditions can be associated with synchronization errors that can result in one process interfering with another process and possibly introduce a vulnerability. Frequently, a potential outcome of a race condition leaves the program in an unstable or invalid state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="97176">race condition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241534">വര്‍ഗ്ഗ സ്ഥിതി</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8026_149177_1877852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any characteristic of text, such as font, size, style, color, or effect such as subscript or superscript.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149177">text attributes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1877852">ടെക്‌സ്റ്റ് ആട്രിബ്യൂട്ടുകള്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8027_141601_1241535"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file in portable executable (PE) file format that can be loaded into memory and executed by the operating system loader.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141601">executable file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241535">നിര്‍വ്വഹണക്ഷമമായ ഫയല്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8027_141602_1241535"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file in portable executable (PE) file format that can be loaded into memory and executed by the operating system loader.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141602">executable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241535">നിര്‍വ്വഹണക്ഷമമായ ഫയല്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="803_44794_1228909"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The work area on a computer screen that simulates the top of an actual desk. The desktop contains the Recycle Bin and other icons (shortcuts to programs, files, folders, and various types of documents such as letters, reports, or pictures) that you can arrange on the electronic desktop just as you would arrange real objects on top of a desk.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44794">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228909">ഡെസ്ക്ടോപ്പ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="803_44794_2244252"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The work area on a computer screen that simulates the top of an actual desk. The desktop contains the Recycle Bin and other icons (shortcuts to programs, files, folders, and various types of documents such as letters, reports, or pictures) that you can arrange on the electronic desktop just as you would arrange real objects on top of a desk.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44794">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2244252">ഡെസ്ക്‌ടോപ്പ്</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8030_37385_1241155"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To join sequentially (for example, to combine the two strings "hello" and "there" into the single string "hello there").</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="37385">concatenate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1241155">ബന്ധിപ്പിക്കുക</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8036_116444_489661"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A horizontal window at the bottom of a parent window in which an application can display various kinds of status information. The status bar can be divided into parts to display more than one type of information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116444">status bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489661">അവസ്ഥാ ബാര്‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8040_149410_489902"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query that uses the UNION operator to combine the results of two or more select queries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149410">union query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ml-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="489902">യൂണിയന്‍ ചോദ്യം</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8042_187011_1241156"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A system that defines a specific and reusable configuration of applications and other systems as members. You can configure these members and describe the communication pathways between them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="187011">application system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><lan